=== SUMMARY ===
term_m has a genuine O(sqrt(n))-scale Gaussian envelope: the local decay rate c := -log(term_m/term_{m-1})*n/m stabilizes (in n) to an O(1), gamma-dependent constant as n grows, at fixed small m -- i.e. term_m ~ exp(-c m^2/(2n)) for m=O(sqrt(n)), the SAME scaling order (sqrt(n)) as the original A_k ~ exp(-beta k^2/n) profile. The swap does not reduce the characteristic scale of the sum -- see fitted c vs beta above.
